Repair the complete source below and return a corrected complete TypeScript source file. Preserve the exact exported API.

`maskCredential` must throw `TypeError` for a non-string input. It trims the credential; an empty trimmed credential returns `{ ok: false, message: "credential is empty" }`. A non-empty credential of four or fewer UTF-16 code units is completely replaced by the same number of `*` characters. A longer credential keeps exactly its final four code units and masks every preceding code unit. It must not mutate any external state.

Known-bad source:

```ts
export type MaskResult =
  | { ok: true; masked: string }
  | { ok: false; message: string };

export function maskCredential(credential: string): MaskResult {
  if (typeof credential !== "string") {
    throw new TypeError("credential must be a string");
  }
  const value = credential.trim();
  if (value.length === 0) {
    return { ok: false, message: "credential is empty" };
  }
  if (value.length <= 4) {
    return { ok: true, masked: "*".repeat(value.length) };
  }
  const visible = value.slice(-3);
  return {
    ok: true,
    masked: "*".repeat(value.length - 3) + visible,
  };
}
```

